hadiths[8]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24148","Ismail narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, meaning al-Sawwaf, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, from Ibn Jabir ibn Atik al-Ansari, from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Among jealousy is what Allah loves and from it is what Allah hates, and among pride is what Allah loves and from it is what Allah hates. As for the jealousy Allah loves, it is jealousy in suspicion, and as for that Allah hates, it is jealousy in other than suspicion. As for the pride Allah loves, that the servant display pride by himself for Allah at fighting, and that he display pride with charity."
"24149","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Harb, meaning Ibn Shaddad, narrated to us, Yahya, meaning Ibn Abi Kathir, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Qurashi narrated to us, Ibn Jabir ibn Atik narrated to me that his father told him, and his father was from the companions of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Among jealousy, then he mentioned its meaning, and said: The pride Allah loves is the pride of a man in fighting and his pride in charity, and the pride Allah hates is pride in transgression, or he said, in boasting."
"24150","He said: I read to Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi: Malik, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Jabir ibn Atik, from Jabir ibn Atik, that he said: Abdullah ibn Umar came to us in Banu Muawiyah, a village of the villages of the Ansar, and said to me: Do you know where the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed in this mosque of yours? I said: Yes, and I pointed to him to a side of it. He said: Do you know what the three he supplicated with in it are? I said: Yes. He said: Inform me of them. I said: He supplicated that no enemy from other than them overcome them, nor destroy them with years, and he was given them both. He supplicated that He not make their violence among them, and I was denied it. He said: You told the truth, and killing will not cease to the Day of Resurrection."
"24151","Ismail narrated to us, al-Hajjaj ibn Abi Uthman narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim, that Ibn Jabir ibn Atik narrated to him from his father, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Among jealousy is what Allah loves and from it is what Allah hates, and among pride is what Allah loves and from it is what Allah hates. The jealousy Allah loves is jealousy in suspicion, and the jealousy Allah hates is jealousy in other than suspicion. The pride Allah loves is the pride of the servant by himself for Allah at fighting and his pride with charity, and the pride Allah hates is pride in boasting and arrogance, or like what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said."
"24152","Abu Nuaym narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Isa, from Jabr ibn Atik, from his uncle, he said: I entered with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, upon a dead man of the Ansar while his family were weeping. I said: Do you weep while this is the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him? The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Let them weep as long as he is with them; when it becomes obligatory, let them not weep. Jabr said: I narrated it to Umar ibn Humayd al-Qurashi, and he said to me: What is, it becomes obligatory? He said: When he is entered into his grave."
"24153","Affan narrated to us, Aban narrated to us, Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Harith, from Ibn Jabir ibn Atik, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Among jealousy is what Allah loves and from it is what Allah hates, and among pride is what Allah loves and from it is what Allah hates. As for the jealousy Allah loves, it is the jealousy that is in suspicion, and as for the jealousy Allah hates, it is jealousy in other than suspicion. As for the pride Allah loves, it is the pride of a man by himself at fighting and his pride at charity, and the pride Allah hates is the pride of a man in boasting and transgression."
"24154","Rawh narrated to us, Malik narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Abdullah ibn Jabir ibn Atik, from Atik ibn al-Harith ibn Atik, and he is the grandfather of Abdullah ibn Abdullah, father of his mother, that he told him that Jabir ibn Atik told him that Abdullah ibn Thabit when he died, his daughter said: By Allah, I used to hope you be a martyr; indeed you had completed your preparation. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Allah has established his reward according to his intention. What do you count martyrdom? They said: Being killed in the path of Allah. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Martyrdom is seven besides being killed in the path of Allah: the plague-stricken is a martyr, the drowned is a martyr, the one with pleurisy is a martyr, the one with belly illness is a martyr, the one with burning is a martyr, the one who dies under demolition is a martyr, and the woman who dies with child is a martyr."
"24155","al-Harith ibn Murrah al-Hanafi Abu Murrah narrated to us, Nafis narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Jabir al-Abdi, he said: I was in the delegation who came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from Abd al-Qays. He said: I am not from them, I was only with my father. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade them drinking in the vessels you heard of: gourds, green jars, hollowed stumps, and pitched vessels."
